C4 — no-target byte-identity vs master: FAIL
  Probe zz_probe_notarget_test.go builds the view from the metrics sentinel
  (models.DashboardMetrics{HasCombinedTarget:false, LivingTargetTotal:0,
  HealthcareTargetTotal:0}) via BuildBudgetVerdict and renders
  "dashboard-verdict-bar" to a file. Run in the branch copy and in a `git worktree
  add ... master` checkout of the same repo copy:
    branch: wrote 1007 bytes    master: wrote 998 bytes
    `cmp branch.html master.html` -> "differ: byte 651, line 12"
    md5: 802a82223232712eb5e0fa1fe09c51dc (branch) vs c2313cc5f1b09c7cae09be70687a17fc (master)
  `diff -u master.html branch.html | cat -A` shows exactly one added line:
      @@ -9,6 +9,7 @@
                   </div>$
      +        $
           </div>$
  i.e. the branch emits 9 extra bytes (8 spaces + newline) in the no-target case.
  Cause: web/templates/components/dashboard-verdict-bar.html lines 25 and 42 add
  `{{if $v.HasTarget}}` / `{{end}}` on their own source lines with no whitespace
  trim markers, so the surrounding newline+indent survives when the branch is not
  taken. No text/markup difference — whitespace only, no visual effect — but the
  written criterion (brief C4; W-RUN-SPEC W4 requirement 4, "the banner is
  byte-identical to today") is not met, and the command above demonstrates it.
  To fix: trim markers on those two actions (e.g. `{{if $v.HasTarget}}` ->
  `{{- if $v.HasTarget}}` and `{{end}}` -> `{{- end}}`) so the false branch emits
  nothing. Note also that the worker's own "no target ..." render subtest asserts
  only the ABSENCE of the new strings; it does not assert byte-identity, so it
  cannot catch this.

